THIRD-PARTY DATA

The MIT terms above cover this project's own code and documentation. The
bundled evaluation suites in `suites/` contain samples redistributed from
public benchmark datasets, each under its own licence. Both are MIT-licensed
and so compatible with the terms above; their attribution notices follow.
Provenance, selection seeds and per-file details are in `suites/SOURCE.md`.

suites/reasoning.jsonl -- 500 items from the GSM8K test split.
    Cobbe, Kosaraju, Bavarian, Chen, Jun, Kaiser, Plappert, Tworek, Hilton,
    Nakano, Hesse & Schulman, "Training Verifiers to Solve Math Word
    Problems", arXiv:2110.14168 (2021).
    Distributed by OpenAI at huggingface.co/datasets/openai/gsm8k under the
    MIT Licence.

suites/knowledge.jsonl -- 500 items from the MMLU test split.
    Hendrycks, Burns, Basart, Zou, Mazeika, Song & Steinhardt, "Measuring
    Massive Multitask Language Understanding", arXiv:2009.03300 (2021).
    Distributed at huggingface.co/datasets/cais/mmlu under the MIT Licence.
    Copyright (c) 2020 Dan Hendrycks (per github.com/hendrycks/test).

suites/instruction.jsonl contains prompts authored for this repository; it is
covered by the MIT terms above.

No code from any third-party repository is included in this project. In
particular, the reference implementation accompanying Kübler et al. (2026)
at github.com/amazon-science/LLM-Accuracy-Stats is licensed CC BY-NC 4.0,
which would be incompatible with these terms; the statistical method here was
implemented from the paper's description. See `quantcheck/stats.py`.
